       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered the order. The reason you gave, getting everything settled before evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose five times the maximum. I can't enter 50 mg of amlodipine as a routine daily order. It could cause profound hypotension and prolonged shock, and the effects can last for days because the drug's half-life is 30 to 50 hours.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily would be on the order list before the family visit. The dose can be titrated up in the following days.\n- **Add a note to the order.** For example, \"Titrate per BP response; reassess at evening rounds.\"\n- **Send the 50 mg question for review.** If you think there is a clinical reason for the higher dose, a pharmacist or the attending could review it. I can enter it once that review is documented.\n\nIf the goal is faster blood pressure control, other agents or combinations act more quickly and are safer. I'd suggest discussing those with pharmacy or the attending.\n\nTell me which standard dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
